Sometimes it returns the IIS server info, not the client PC.


---

✅ Correct Way to Get CLIENT IP

Use this:

string clientIP = Request.ServerVariables["HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR"];

if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(clientIP))
{
    clientIP = Request.ServerVariables["REMOTE_ADDR"];
}

✔ Why?

HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR → real client IP (if behind proxy)

REMOTE_ADDR → fallback



---

✅ Get CLIENT HOSTNAME (PC Name)

string clientHost = System.Net.Dns.GetHostEntry(clientIP).HostName;

⚠️ Note:

This only works if:

Network allows reverse DNS

Client PC is registered in DNS


Otherwise, it may fail or return server name



---

✅ Best Reliable Method (Recommended)

👉 Use JavaScript to get client machine name/IP

Because server-side C# cannot reliably get client hostname.


